  "query_preview": "..The start of the long term looks to remain active with the \nlow pressure continuing to persist. This will allow for clouds and \nprecipitation to continue to impact the area. This low eventually \ndissipates while a stronger low looks to pass south of the area and \nhigh pressure builds in Canada. Behind this low, high pressure is \nexpected to move in to the Gulf behind this stronger low which may \nallow for us to see a break Sunday evening into Monday morning. \nHeaded into the start of next week, ensemble guidance wants to bring \nanother low into the western Gulf. The main difference between EPS \nand GEFS guidance is where this low comes from. EPS wants to bring a \nlow up from the south on Monday and have it merge with a low that is \nexpected to persist in the Bering Sea before moving towards the Cook \nInlet area Tuesday. This low then tracks into Prince William Sound \nTuesday evening into Wednesday. GEFS guidance wants to bring the low \nfrom the Bering Sea on Monday and track it across the Alaska \nPeninsula and Cook Inlet before moving remaining offshore near \nPrince William Sound.",
